<?= flash_messages() ?>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-body">
    <h4 class="card-title mb-1">Turn on automatic CPL submission</h4>
    <p class="text-muted small">
      Once ON, the system builds the daily and the monthly file by itself and uploads them to Creditinfo as <strong>live (L702)</strong> files, with no second
      person approving each one. Files that have any blocking problem, or any unanswered instalment, are held back and the staff are e-mailed. Nothing is sent
      while the submission environment in CPL Settings is not Production.
    </p>

    <?php foreach ($blockers as $b): ?>
      <div class="alert alert-danger py-2 small"><?= e($b) ?></div>
    <?php endforeach; ?>

    <div class="alert alert-info py-2 small">
      <strong>Who is e-mailed about problems (counts and a link only, never names or loan numbers):</strong>
      <?php if ($recipients === []): ?>
        nobody with an e-mail address yet - you will be added automatically when you turn it on, if you have an e-mail address.
      <?php else: ?>
        <?= e(implode(', ', array_map(static fn (array $u): string => (string) $u['name'] . ' <' . (string) $u['email'] . '>', $recipients))) ?>
      <?php endif; ?>
    </div>

    <?php
      $cronMissing = !empty($cron['any_missing']);
      $cronStale = !$cronMissing && (!empty($cron['daily']['stale']) || !empty($cron['monthly']['stale']));
    ?>
    <?php if ($cronMissing): ?>
      <div class="alert alert-danger py-2 small">
        <strong>The scheduled job has never reported in.</strong>
        <?= $cron['daily']['last'] === null ? 'The daily job has never run. ' : '' ?><?= $cron['monthly']['last'] === null ? 'The monthly job has never run. ' : '' ?>
        Automatic submission only works when the technical team has installed both cron lines (see below). Without them, switching it on sends nothing.
      </div>
    <?php elseif ($cronStale): ?>
      <div class="alert alert-danger py-2 small"><strong>A scheduled job has not reported for more than <?= (int) \App\Services\CplAutoSubmissionService::HEARTBEAT_STALE_HOURS ?> hours.</strong> Nothing would be sent until the technical team fixes the crontab.</div>
    <?php endif; ?>
    <p class="small text-muted">Cron lines (server time, installed by the technical team):
      <code>30 6 * * * cd /path/to/app &amp;&amp; php bin/cpl_auto_submit.php --daily</code> and
      <code>0 7 * * * cd /path/to/app &amp;&amp; php bin/cpl_auto_submit.php --monthly</code>.
    </p>

    <div class="alert alert-warning">
      <strong>Please read: the monthly file is not the full historic loan book.</strong><br>
      <?= e($panel['warning']) ?>
      <br>
      Tracked right now by the Loan Questions: <strong><?= (int) $panel['tracked_loans'] ?></strong> approved and paid-out loan(s);
      applications still awaiting an answer: <strong><?= (int) $panel['awaiting_answer'] ?></strong>.
    </div>

    <h5 class="mt-3">What the first daily file would contain</h5>
    <ul class="small">
      <li><strong><?= (int) $preview['registrations'] ?></strong> new registration(s) (loans paid out and not yet reported)<?= $preview['oldest_paid_out'] ? ', the oldest paid out on ' . e($preview['oldest_paid_out']) : '' ?></li>
      <li><strong><?= (int) $preview['closures'] ?></strong> closure(s) (loans paid in full)</li>
      <li><strong><?= (int) $preview['blocked'] ?></strong> loan(s) that cannot be reported yet<?= (int) $preview['blocked'] > 0 ? ' - they are left out of the file (the rest is sent) and tried again every day' : '' ?></li>
      <li>The monthly catch-up: <strong><?= (int) $preview['monthly_months'] ?></strong> month end(s) not sent yet, oldest first; the latest would hold <strong><?= (int) $preview['monthly_records'] ?></strong> record(s)</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-muted small">
      The first live file of each kind may not be more than 20% bigger than the numbers shown here (<?= (int) $preview['daily_records'] ?> daily, <?= (int) $preview['monthly_records'] ?> monthly record(s)); a bigger one is held back and the staff are e-mailed.
    </p>
    <p class="text-muted small">
      If some of those loans were already registered with Creditinfo another way, choose below the first pay-out date to register from; earlier loans are then
      not registered by the daily file (their closures are still reported). <a href="<?= url('/reports/cpl-export/auto/enable?since=') ?>">Reset</a>
    </p>

    <form method="get" action="<?= url('/reports/cpl-export/auto/enable') ?>" class="row g-2 mb-3">
      <div class="col-md-4">
        <label class="form-label small">Preview: only loans paid out on or after</label>
        <input type="date" name="since" class="form-control form-control-sm" value="<?= e($since) ?>">
      </div>
      <div class="col-md-3 align-self-end"><button type="submit" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary">Update preview</button></div>
    </form>

    <form method="post" action="<?= url('/reports/cpl-export/auto/enable') ?>">
      <?= csrf_field() ?>
      <input type="hidden" name="since" value="<?= e($since) ?>">
      <input type="hidden" name="preview_daily" value="<?= (int) $preview['daily_records'] ?>">
      <input type="hidden" name="preview_monthly" value="<?= (int) $preview['monthly_records'] ?>">
      <div class="form-check mb-3">
        <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" name="acknowledge_completeness" value="1" id="ack" required>
        <label class="form-check-label" for="ack">
          I understand that the monthly file built from the Loan Questions is <strong>not the full historic loan book</strong>: the active loans still
          managed in the old SolidFin system are not included and are not reported by this automatic submission.
        </label>
      </div>
      <div class="form-check mb-3">
        <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" name="acknowledge_standing_approval" value="1" id="ack2" required>
        <label class="form-check-label" for="ack2">
          <strong>I give the standing approval.</strong> From now on live files are uploaded by the scheduled job without a second person approving each one;
          my name and the time are recorded on every file. The approval ends when I turn the switch off, or when the submission environment, the supplier
          reference, the recipient or the SFTP destination changes, or when Creditinfo's server refuses the login.
        </label>
      </div>
      <?php if ($cronMissing): ?>
      <div class="form-check mb-3">
        <input class="form-check-input" type="checkbox" name="acknowledge_no_heartbeat" value="1" id="ack3" required>
        <label class="form-check-label" for="ack3">I know the scheduled job has never reported in: nothing is sent until the cron lines are installed.</label>
      </div>
      <?php endif; ?>
      <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary" <?= $blockers !== [] ? 'disabled' : '' ?> onclick="return confirm('Turn ON automatic submission? Live files will then be uploaded to Creditinfo by the scheduled job.');">Turn automatic submission ON</button>
      <a href="<?= url('/reports/cpl-export/batches') ?>" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Cancel</a>
    </form>
  </div>
</div>
